; dialogesc.eval - Esc backs out ONE layer, whatever is open (code-review C81).
; Judged by tools/EditorTest.py phase 24, on its scratch world.
;
; Every Esc here is a KEY (`presskey esc`): pressed and let go in the frame
; after the line, so it goes through the frame's own input path - the dialog's
; Update, the editor's ladder, the travel screen's - and not a handler called
; by name, which would skip the very ordering under test. A drop-down is opened
; as a press on its face opens it (`... popup <n>`, at the dialog's next
; Update); each status line between the keys reads where things stand.
;
;   --- inspector ---  the warrior at 23,9 made a Caster (a live edit), its
;                      Facing list opened: the first Esc closes the list and
;                      leaves the dialog and the edit; the second cancels the
;                      dialog, and reopened the warrior is what it was.
;   --- level ---      Level settings, dust typed in (previewed live), the
;                      material list opened: the first Esc keeps the dialog and
;                      the dust; the second closes it and puts the dust back.
;   --- generate ---   the Generate dialog's Style list: the first Esc keeps
;                      the dialog, the second closes it.
;   --- newworld ---   the New world dialog's level list: the same.
;   --- asset ---      the create dialog (decorations' "+ New..."), which had no
;                      Esc at all: its source list takes the first, the dialog
;                      the second.
;   --- levellist ---  a brush armed, then the toolbar's level list: the first
;                      Esc closes only the list, the second puts the brush
;                      down, the third closes the editor.
;   --- world ---      the world editor with a terrain brush armed: the first
;                      Esc puts the brush down, the second pauses, the third
;                      resumes on the travel screen.

logecho on
reset
timescale 0
echo --- inspector ---
editor inspect 23 9
editor inspector
editor inspector archetype caster
editor inspector popup 0
editor inspector popup
presskey esc
editor inspector
editor inspector popup
presskey esc
editor inspector
editor inspect 23 9
editor inspector
editor inspector esc
echo --- level ---
dust
editor levelsettings open
editor levelsettings dust 0.31
dust
editor levelsettings popup 0
editor levelsettings
presskey esc
editor levelsettings
dust
presskey esc
editor levelsettings
dust
echo --- generate ---
generate dialog
generate dialog tab 3
generate dialog popup 0
generate dialog popup
presskey esc
generate dialog popup
presskey esc
generate dialog popup
echo --- newworld ---
worlds newdialog
worlds newdialog popup 0
worlds newdialog popup
presskey esc
worlds newdialog popup
presskey esc
worlds newdialog popup
echo --- asset ---
editor newasset decorations
editor newasset popup 0
editor newasset
presskey esc
editor newasset
presskey esc
editor newasset
echo --- levellist ---
editor arm decorations column
editor levellist open
editor levellist
presskey esc
editor levellist
presskey esc
editor levellist
presskey esc
editor levellist
echo --- world ---
worldedit on
worldmap on
terrainbrush moor
presskey esc
terrainbrush
state
presskey esc
state
presskey esc
state
worldmap off
worldedit off
echo --- end ---
